James inquired about a disease that spreads radially, suggesting a strong environmental infection pathway rather than a human travel-related spread. I confirmed this pattern is characteristic of diseases like cholera, which spreads through contaminated water, leading to a radial spread from the source. In contrast, diseases transmitted directly between people, like COVID-19, often follow human travel routes. I emphasized the importance of understanding these transmission modes for effective control and prevention strategies and offered to discuss specific diseases further if he had one in mind.
